{% extends layout %}
{#
  Privacy Policy under the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013. The text is version
  controlled here, and its last-updated date is in CattoLearning\Legal\LegalDocuments: change the date
  whenever this text changes (no version numbers, owner 2026-10-17). What it says is stored must match the schema, and the cookie
  names and lifetimes must match the instance defaults (LegalDocumentsTest checks .env.example).
#}
{% block page_body %}
	{% set ph_kicker = 'Legal' %}
	{% set ph_title = legal.title %}
	{% set ph_lead = 'What personal information ' ~ supplier.trading_name ~ ' collects, why, who receives it and how long it is kept.' %}
	{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}
	{% set legal_intro = 'This policy explains how personal information is handled on this site, as the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA) requires.' %}
	{% set legal_sections = [
		{id: 'responsible-party', label: 'Who is responsible'},
		{id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect'},
		{id: 'why', label: 'Why we use it'},
		{id: 'age', label: 'Age'},
		{id: 'identity', label: 'Identity verification, certificates and transcripts'},
		{id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies'},
		{id: 'who-receives', label: 'Who receives your information'},
		{id: 'retention', label: 'How long we keep it'},
		{id: 'security', label: 'How we protect it'},
		{id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights'},
	] %}
	<section class="cl-page-section">
		{% include '@platform/partials/legal-document-head.html.twig' %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'responsible-party'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '1. Who is responsible'}) }}
			<p>The responsible party under POPIA is {{ supplier.legal_name }}, {{ supplier.legal_form_phrase }} trading as {{ supplier.trading_name }}. The Information Officer is {{ supplier.information_officer }}.</p>
			{{ ui('data.key-value-list', {items: [
				{label: 'Responsible party', value: supplier.legal_name ~ ', trading as ' ~ supplier.trading_name},
				{label: 'Information Officer', value: supplier.information_officer},
				{label: 'Physical address', value: supplier.physical_address},
				{label: 'Telephone', value: supplier.phone},
				{label: 'Email address', value: supplier.email},
				{label: 'Website', value: supplier.website},
			]}) }}
			<p>We may change this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it last changed. If a change affects how we use information we already hold about you, we will email you before it takes effect.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'what-we-collect'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '2. What we collect'}) }}
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Your account.</strong> Your names, your display name, the name for your certificate and your email addresses. If you give them: your date of birth, gender, cell number, identification number, profile picture and links to your social media. Your role on the site and the company you belong to, if any. Your account reference, which the site gives your account when it is made. Checkout asks for your first name, last name and cell number.</li>
				<li><strong>Billing details.</strong> Your billing name, organisation, tax number and address. They are copied into each order you place.</li>
				<li><strong>Orders and payments.</strong> Your orders, what you bought and the prices, your invoices, receipts and credit notes, and each payment's method, amount and reference. For a direct EFT, the bank reference and date we confirmed it with. Any refund request, what you wrote in it and our decision, and any refund and the reason for it. For money back by EFT, the bank details you give us are used only to make that payment and are not stored on this site. We do not receive or store card numbers or banking login details.</li>
				<li><strong>Your wallet.</strong> Each amount of wallet credit added to your wallet, spent or expired, with its date and expiry date, and the reminders we email you before credit expires.</li>
				<li><strong>Emails about your payments.</strong> An email we send you about a payment, a refund or your wallet is recorded with the transaction it is about.</li>
				<li><strong>Learning records.</strong> The courses you are enrolled on, your progress, every answer you give in an assessment and how long you took to answer, your marks and results, course requests and their notes, and your certificates.</li>
				<li><strong>Reviews.</strong> Your rating and what you write. Once a review is approved it is shown publicly with your first name and the first letter of your surname.</li>
				<li><strong>Activity log.</strong> A record of actions on your account, such as signing in or changing your details. The activity log stores the IP address of each recorded action. You can see your own activity in your account.</li>
				<li><strong>Sessions.</strong> Each browser session and each sign-in session stores a hashed IP address and your browser's user agent. This applies to every visitor, signed in or not. A request for a sign-in link also stores a hashed IP address.</li>
				<li><strong>Analytics events.</strong> Our own record of events such as a course page being viewed, a checkout being started or a course being bought. An event stores your user number if you are signed in, or a random visitor number kept only for your browser session, with the course or order concerned and any campaign tags in the address you arrived by. Analytics events store neither an IP address nor a user agent.</li>
				<li><strong>Messages.</strong> A message you send through the contact form is emailed to us. It is not stored in the website's database.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>If you belong to a company, your Company Administrator can see your name, email address and role, the courses you are on and your status, progress and dates on them. The company also sees totals for each course with an average result.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'why'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '3. Why we use it'}) }}
			<p>We use personal information only for these purposes:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>to give you an account, sign you in and give you access to your courses</li>
				<li>to take orders, confirm payments, make refunds and issue invoices, receipts and credit notes</li>
				<li>to mark your assessments, record your results and issue certificates and transcripts</li>
				<li>to verify your identity before a certificate or transcript is issued</li>
				<li>to let a company manage the courses of its staff members</li>
				<li>to keep the site secure and to investigate misuse</li>
				<li>to measure which courses are viewed and bought</li>
				<li>to answer your questions and complaints</li>
				<li>to keep the financial records the law requires</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'age'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '4. Age'}) }}
			<p>Learners must be 18 or older. A learner under 18 needs the consent of a parent or guardian.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'identity'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '5. Identity verification, certificates and transcripts'}) }}
			<p>You may take a course under any name you choose.</p>
			<p>A certificate is issued to every learner who completes every assessment in a course, whether or not they pass. A certificate and a transcript are issued only after your identity has been verified. Both state your name exactly as it appears on your official identity document.</p>
			<p>To be verified:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>a South African learner supplies their RSA ID number and a copy of their ID document</li>
				<li>a learner from another country supplies their passport number and a picture of their passport</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We review the document, download it for secure offline storage and then delete it from the website. The website keeps only your ID or passport number, your verified name, and who verified it and when. Offline copies are kept for 5 years.</p>
			<p>The purpose is to protect the credibility of certificates and transcripts.</p>
			<p>A certificate states only that you took the course. It shows your verified name, the course, the date, the certificate number, the accreditation and the provider. It shows no grade. A transcript records each module assessment mark, the final assessment mark and the overall grade, which is 50% module assessments and 50% final assessment.</p>
			{% embed ui_template('feedback.notice') with {props: ui_props('feedback.notice', {tone: 'info', heading: 'Certificates and transcripts are public'})} %}
{% block body %}
				Anyone who has the link to your certificate or transcript, or its number, can view it without signing in. They will see your name. On a transcript they will also see your marks and your grade.
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'cookies'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '6. Cookies', summary: 'The site sets three cookies. None is an advertising or third-party tracking cookie.'}) }}
			<ul>
				<li><strong>catto_learning_web</strong> keeps your browser session: your cart, your checkout steps, form protection and the random analytics visitor number. It is set for every visitor. It ends when you close your browser, and its record on the server is removed after 24 hours without use.</li>
				<li><strong>catto_learning_session</strong> keeps you signed in. It is set when you sign in. It lasts 24 hours and is renewed while you use the site.</li>
				<li><strong>cl_palette</strong> remembers the colour palette the site is shown in. It is set when a theme that offers colour palettes is shown. It lasts 1 year.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>The site also keeps small display settings in your browser's local storage, such as the chosen palette and the position of the menu. They stay in your browser.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'who-receives'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '7. Who receives your information'}) }}
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Stitch, for payments.</strong> Payments are processed by Stitch. Card details are entered on Stitch's secure page and never reach this site. For a bank payment through Stitch, you enter your banking login on Stitch's page, not on this site. Stitch may process personal information outside South Africa.</li>
				<li><strong>OVHcloud, for hosting.</strong> The site and its database are hosted by OVHcloud on a server in Canada. Your personal information is therefore stored outside South Africa.</li>
				<li><strong>Email.</strong> Email is sent from the site's own mail server on the same host.</li>
				<li><strong>Google Fonts.</strong> When the site is shown in the Gilded Noir or Light Default theme, your browser loads fonts from Google. Google then receives your IP address.</li>
				<li><strong>YouTube.</strong> Some course videos are embedded from youtube-nocookie.com. When you open a page with such a video, your browser connects to YouTube.</li>
				<li><strong>Your company.</strong> Your Company Administrator sees the information set out in <a href="#what-we-collect">section 2</a>.</li>
				<li><strong>The public.</strong> An approved review, and a certificate or transcript, as <a href="#what-we-collect">section 2</a> and <a href="#identity">section 5</a> explain.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We also disclose personal information when the law requires it.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'retention'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '8. How long we keep it'}) }}
			{{ ui('data.key-value-list', {items: [
				{label: 'Orders and transaction records', value: 'At least 5 years'},
				{label: 'Activity log', value: '5 years'},
				{label: 'Analytics events', value: '5 years'},
				{label: 'Offline copies of identity documents', value: '5 years'},
				{label: 'Sign-in links', value: '30 minutes'},
				{label: 'Sessions', value: '24 hours'},
			]}) }}
			<p>Your account details, learning records, certificates and reviews are kept for as long as you have an account.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true, id: 'security'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '9. How we protect it'}) }}
			<ul>
				<li>The site has no passwords. You sign in with a one-time link that expires after 30 minutes.</li>
				<li>Sign-in links and sign-in sessions are stored only in hashed form.</li>
				<li>Card details and banking logins are entered on Stitch's pages and never reach this site.</li>
				<li>Identity documents are deleted from the website after they have been verified.</li>
				<li>You can see your active sessions in your account and end any of them.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>If a security breach affects your personal information, we will tell you and the Information Regulator as POPIA requires.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

		{% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'your-rights'})} %}
{% block surface_body %}
			{{ ui('layout.section-head', {heading: '10. Your rights'}) }}
			<p>Under POPIA you have the right to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>ask whether we hold personal information about you and ask for a copy of it</li>
				<li>ask us to correct or delete personal information that is inaccurate, out of date, excessive or unlawfully obtained</li>
				<li>ask us to delete personal information we no longer have a right to keep</li>
				<li>object to the processing of your personal information on reasonable grounds</li>
				<li>withdraw a consent you have given</li>
				<li>complain to the Information Regulator</li>
			</ul>
			<p>You can correct most of your details yourself in your account profile. To exercise any other right, contact the Information Officer, {{ supplier.information_officer }}:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>email <a href="mailto:{{ supplier.email }}">{{ supplier.email }}</a></li>
				<li>telephone <a href="{{ supplier.phone_href }}">{{ supplier.phone }}</a></li>
				<li>post to {{ supplier.physical_address }}</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We may ask you to prove who you are before we act on a request. Records that the law requires us to keep, such as order and transaction records, cannot be deleted while that duty lasts.</p>
			<p>You have the right to complain to the Information Regulator at <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://inforegulator.org.za</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
	</section>
{% endblock %}
